{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/37716-wraith-why-no-pod","id":37716,"title":"Wraith: Why no PoD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-26T22:47:07-08:00","id":37716,"title":"Wraith: Why no PoD?","content":"I've snagged Wraith: The Great War and Orpheus from DriveThruRPG in hardcover print copies, but there's no option for the Wraith core other than as a PDF. Is there any particular reason for this? I'm the sort comforted by having a book in my hands, and it's funny to not have the option for a core rulebook when a number of supplements have it. It's a hard book to track down, and most used copies are fairly battered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T22:59:19-08:00","id":37721,"title":"","content":"Reformatting the old books takes time. And while the folks in-charge have been committed to putting in the effort, getting through the old catalog is slow going with all the new stuff in the works.<br /> <br /> I'd personally wager that getting the older books PoD ready isn't exactly a hugely profitable endeavor. Someone's gotta do it, and they can't possibly be expecting to even break even for the extra sales it might generate.<br /> <br /> As for what order things have been done in? I have no clue. I'm sure there's lots of factors (esp. the quality of the PDFs of the older books). Given the massive cWOD catalog, it's possible certain books just got skipped for some reason and nobody's had time to go through the &quot;do this one later&quot; pile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T23:27:32-08:00","id":37733,"title":"","content":"There's plenty of Wraith core books to be bought used in good condition off of Amazon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T00:56:05-08:00","id":37748,"title":"","content":"Yeeeep. And they're cheap. I got mine for like $10 + Shipping. Whups, just checked and they went up in price. Maybe the announcement of Wraith20 bumped the prices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T06:05:42-08:00","id":37813,"title":"","content":"Actually that's because the sale ended. Wraith, Orpheus and Geist were on sale until the end of Boxing Day.<br /> <br /> I myself picked up the Orpheus line on PDF yesterday, excluding the novel, and I have to say I was pleasantly surprised by the quality of it. Anyone who's bought some CWoD PDFs know the quality can vary, some are excellent quality akin to the NWoD PDFs while others are simply just scans of the books, a few of which are just abysmal. All six Orpheus books while not the highest quality CWoD books they are at the level just beneath that. Though to be fair part of the quality issues they suffer from is more because of the format of some of pages than anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T14:30:35-08:00","id":38012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/37716-wraith-why-no-pod?p=37813#post37813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually that's because the sale ended. Wraith, Orpheus and Geist were on sale until the end of Boxing Day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, the PDF sale still has 16 hours to go as of this post.<br /> <br /> The Wraith core book has a number of issues with the original production files that make it really difficult to make a PoD version. So many issues that we're likely going to have to scan it instead of making a OEF version of the book.<br /> <br /> -Matt<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T18:23:08-08:00","id":38097,"title":"","content":"Is it halftoning, or a spotcolor process? Or is it the production file type doesn't transfer to the file type LS needs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div a